James outlined a plan to develop a "Planner" that serves as an abstraction for model and tool selection in an AI system. The goal is to maximize user utility by balancing factors like expected positive outcomes, quality, cost, and latency. Key components include a public API for model and tool registration and a mechanism to select execution plans. The discussion covered the public API for registering models and tools and emphasized the importance of maintaining clear versioning to avoid overwriting materially changed items. Various models, tools, and plans will be registered, which will later be used to select the appropriate responders based on user context and registered evidence.
